# A CPU-only Ollama for this stack.
#
# The upstream `ollama/ollama` image ships every GPU backend Ollama supports — four CUDA trees
# (`cuda_v12`, `cuda_v13`, `cuda_jetpack5`, `cuda_jetpack6`) totalling about 3.6 GB. This project
# runs in Docker Desktop on Apple Silicon, where a container cannot reach an NVIDIA GPU, so none of
# that can ever load and the CPU/ARM runners are what actually execute.
#
# Two things make this work, and the second is the one that matters:
#
#   1. Delete the CUDA trees from the upstream filesystem. Ollama discovers its runners at startup
#      and falls back to CPU when none match, so removing them changes nothing it does here.
#   2. Flatten into `FROM scratch` rather than layering a delete on top. Deleting a file in a later
#      layer removes it from the *filesystem* but leaves the bytes in the layer below, so a plain
#      `RUN rm -rf` would shrink nothing. Copying the cleaned filesystem into a single new layer is
#      what actually returns the space.
#
# `FROM scratch` also discards the upstream metadata, so the ENV, EXPOSE, ENTRYPOINT and CMD below
# re-declare it exactly as the pinned image has it, minus the NVIDIA variables that only mean
# something with the NVIDIA container toolkit present.
#
# To go back to stock upstream, point the `ollama` and `models` services in `docker-compose.yml` at
# `ollama/ollama:0.40.2` again and delete this file.
# The default is the production pin. The M3b model comparison builds a tools-profile server on 0.40.6
# so the spike's local model (tev1:0.8b) never lands in the production volume; a later milestone would
# change the default only if a model-first router is adopted (decision 0003).
ARG OLLAMA_VERSION=0.40.2
FROM ollama/ollama:${OLLAMA_VERSION} AS upstream

RUN rm -rf /usr/lib/ollama/cuda_v12 \
           /usr/lib/ollama/cuda_v13 \
           /usr/lib/ollama/cuda_jetpack5 \
           /usr/lib/ollama/cuda_jetpack6

FROM scratch

COPY --from=upstream / /

ENV PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin \
    OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0:11434

EXPOSE 11434

ENTRYPOINT ["/bin/ollama"]
CMD ["serve"]
